{"type": "tool_call", "n": 65, "ts": 1790153432.7821581, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "TO: Controller\nFROM: Senior Accountant\nRE: US (Halvard Systems Inc., USD) March 2026 vs February 2026 Operating Expense Flux\nDATE: 2026-04-03\n\nSCOPE / METHOD\nPulled period activity for every US expense account (5000-7200) for 2026-02 and 2026-03 from the GL. Threshold for explanation per your request: change > 10% AND > $5,000. Three lines meet both tests. I then pulled ledger detail for those lines. NOTE: my tool-call budget was exhausted mid-investigation; see \"Limitations\" below for exactly what I could not verify.\n\nFLUX TABLE (period activity, USD)\nAcct  Line                         Feb 2026     Mar 2026     $ Chg       % Chg    Explain?\n5000  Hosting & Infrastructure     31,301.80    40,948.20    +9,646.40   +30.8%   YES\n6000  Salaries & Wages            183,800.38   184,465.91      +665.53    +0.4%   no\n6010  Payroll Taxes                14,060.73    14,111.64       +50.91    +0.4%   no\n6100  Rent                         14,500.00    14,500.00         0.00     0.0%   no\n6110  Utilities                       919.82       922.22        +2.40    +0.3%   no\n6200  Software Subscriptions        4,139.80     3,339.50      -800.30   -19.3%   no (<$5k)\n6300  Travel                          785.40     7,158.41    +6,373.01  +811.4%   YES\n6310  Meals & Entertainment           114.32        49.75       -64.57   -56.5%   no (<$5k)\n6320  Training & Conferences          542.56         0.00      -542.56  -100.0%   no (<$5k)\n6400  Marketing Programs            7,898.14    29,686.00   +21,787.86  +275.9%   YES\n6600  Office Supplies                 197.75       281.47       +83.72   +42.3%   no (<$5k)\n6800  Depreciation                  3,425.00         0.00    -3,425.00  -100.0%   no (<$5k) - see note\n6900  Bank Fees                        65.00         0.00       -65.00  -100.0%   no (<$5k) - see note\nAll other expense accounts (5100, 5200, 6020, 6030, 6120, 6410, 6500, 6510, 6520, 6550, 6700, 6950, 7000, 7100, 7200): $0 in both months.\nTotal opex (5000-7200): Feb 261,750.90 -> Mar 295,463.10, +33,712.20 (+12.9%).\n\nEXPLANATIONS\n\n1) 5000 Hosting & Infrastructure: +$9,646.40 (+30.8%) -- DRIVER HOLDS UP\n   Feb: JE-00125 (2026-02-03) Stackline Cloud inv STA-12523, cloud infrastructure - production, $31,301.80 (AP, supported).\n   Mar: JE-00232 (2026-03-03) Stackline Cloud inv STA-98877, cloud infrastructure - production, $31,148.20 (AP, supported).\n        JE-00258 (2026-03-14) Stackline Cloud inv SC-M-2203, one-time data migration, $9,800.00 (AP, supported).\n   The recurring production hosting charge is essentially flat (-$153.60). The entire variance is the $9,800 one-time data migration invoice. Both March entries are AP-sourced with support attached. Non-recurring; expect 5000 to revert to ~$31k in April absent new usage. One judgment item for you: if the migration relates to a capital project it may warrant capitalization review, but as an expense it is properly supported.\n\n2) 6300 Travel: +$6,373.01 (+811%) -- DRIVER DOES NOT HOLD UP\n   Mar detail (5 entries, $7,158.41):\n     JE-00266 03/15 Card - Hilton Garden Inn hotel        $197.45  (supported)\n     JE-00269 03/16 Card - Delta Air Lines airfare        $566.47  (supported)\n     JE-00277 03/21 Card - Uber ground transport           $53.29  (supported)\n     JE-00298 03/27 Card - Uber ground transport           $41.20  (supported)\n     JE-00300 03/29 \"Travel reimbursement - T. Vance\"   $6,300.00  (MANUAL, NO SUPPORT, Dr 6300 / Cr 1000 Cash-Operating)\n   The four card items total $858.41 -- roughly in line with Feb ($785.40). The variance is entirely JE-00300: a $6,300.00 manual journal, round-dollar, posted two days before month-end, booked directly against operating cash, with no expense report, receipts, or approval attached. It is 88% of the month's travel expense and is ~8x the typical monthly run-rate. I could not locate support and could not confirm a matching bank disbursement before my tool budget ran out. I could not log the flag_exception call for the same reason -- please treat this memo as the exception flag. Recommended actions: (a) obtain T. Vance's expense report and receipts; (b) confirm a $6,300 cash outflow actually cleared in 1000 (if not, the entry should be reversed or reclassed to 2100 Accrued Expenses / 1450 Employee Advances as appropriate); (c) if it is a cash advance rather than incurred travel, it belongs in 1450 not 6300. Until supported, I do not consider this variance explained.\n\n3) 6400 Marketing Programs: +$21,787.86 (+276%) -- NOT YET VERIFIED\n   My ledger-detail request for 6400 (Feb and Mar) was rejected because the tool-call budget was exhausted. I cannot cite the driving transactions. Given the size ($21.8k, the largest single-line movement in the flux) this must be completed before sign-off: pull 6400 March entries, confirm each has vendor support (invoice/contract), check for a one-time program spend or a duplicate/mis-period posting, and confirm nothing is prepaid that should sit in 1200.\n\nITEMS BELOW THRESHOLD THAT STILL NEED ATTENTION\n- 6800 Depreciation: $0 in March vs $3,425.00 in Feb (and Jan). The March depreciation entry appears not to have been posted yet. Expected March expense ~ $3,425 (Dr 6800 / Cr 1510). Should be posted before close; this is a close-checklist item, not a real variance.\n- 6900 Bank Fees: $0 in March vs $65 in Jan and Feb. Likely the March bank-fee line has not been booked from the statement yet; check unmatched bank lines in 1000.\n- 6200 Software Subscriptions: -$800 (-19%). Below $ threshold; not investigated.\n- 6320 Training: -$542.56 (-100%). Below $ threshold; Feb had a one-off, March none.\n\nLIMITATIONS / OPEN ITEMS FOR CONTROLLER\n1. 6400 Marketing detail not pulled (budget exhausted) -- open, high priority.\n2. JE-00300 $6,300 unsupported manual travel entry -- open, needs support or reversal; flag_exception could not be filed via tool.\n3. Feb 6300 detail and JE-00300 full transaction detail/bank match not retrieved.\n4. Close checklist not retrieved; March depreciation and bank fee accruals appear outstanding.\nNo journal entries were posted or reversed and no bank lines were matched in the course of this work."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 10}
